{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And if you reject My statutes.</b> Not only do you nullify them, but you reject them." "<b>And if your soul abhors My ordinances.</b> You abhor them as a man induces vomiting with deliberate intent — not because there is reason to reject them, since their rationale is known and sound." "<b>So as not to perform all My commandments.</b> This abhorrence of the ordinances will be only in order to cast off from yourselves the yoke of all the commandments. As the Sages, of blessed memory, said (Sanhedrin 63b): Israel knew that idolatry had no substance in it, yet they worshipped idolatry only in order to permit themselves sexual transgressions publicly. And so the prophet testified, saying (Hosea 5:4): ״לֹא יִתְּנוּ מַעַלְלֵיהֶם לָשׁוּב אֶל אֱלֹהֵיהֶם כִּי רוּחַ זְנוּנִים בְּקִרְבָּם״ — their deeds do not let them return to their Elohim, for a spirit of harlotry is within them." "<b>To break My covenant.</b> In order to be like the rest of the nations that rule in this world without any yoke of Torah and commandments, as He said (Ezekiel 20:32): ״וְהָעֹלָה עַל רוּחֲכֶם הָיוֹ לֹא תִהְיֶה, אֲשֶׁר אַתֶּם אוֹמְרִים נִהְיֶה כַגּוֹיִם כְּמִשְׁפְּחוֹת הָאֲרָצוֹת לְשָׁרֵת עֵץ וָאָבֶן״ — and what arises in your spirit shall not be, namely that you say, 'We will be like the nations, like the families of the lands, to serve wood and stone.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:19.071304101Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}